From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:45:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 123/145] refactor(refinery): extract resolve_merge_strategy
 and resolve_approval_required from merge-push main (gcp-l8td.8)

merge-batch.sh (D1.1) must decide batch eligibility by the same rules the
single-bead lane uses, or the two drift: a member the batch accepts could be a
bead the lane would hand off as a pull request. So the two decisions main made
inline become functions the batch script can call after sourcing this file in
source-only mode.

resolve_merge_strategy <bead-id> reads the bead's metadata.merge_strategy
(default direct), maps pr to mr, and forces mr when existing_pr is set. It
prints the strategy on stdout and the existing_pr notice on stderr, so a caller
can capture the strategy alone. resolve_approval_required is the approval
opt-in case statement, unchanged, setting APPROVAL_REQUIRED.

No behaviour change. main still makes four bead reads (the strategy read moved
into the function), prints the same notice at the same point, and resolves the
approval switch with the same fail-closed case. Every gastown/tests suite
passes at this commit with unchanged assertions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
